         The superseded and rejected ones are what the Consistency Engine will
         need in Phase 3 — hence the flag rather than a separate file.
+
+        `supersede()` appends the replacement without rewriting the old
+        record, so the old record's own `status` field stays `ACTIVE` in the
+        log forever. Reclassification therefore has to happen here, on read,
+        by following the `supersedes` chain: any decision that some other
